  "interpretations": [
    "BRC100 line307 permits SDK trimming and lowercase normalization before namespace checks. Uppercase input therefore has an exact normalized-basket positive control. Minimum five characters, single-space and non-basket-suffix constraints remain separately enforced; the300-versus400 maximum conflict remains unresolved.",
    "Privileged:true absent/four-character/51-character reason requests must be rejected specifically for privilegedReason. A generic unsupported secondary keyring or user denial never passes. No successful privileged authorization or distinct private root is claimed.",
    "Identity override uses otherwise valid derivation inputs. No malformed inactive-field acceptance is assumed.",
    "Discovery name, description and numerical trust are bound to the independently verified signed public settings token. iconUrl remains presentation metadata: require an absolute HTTPS URL, without claiming ownership or image-content authenticity.",
    "All native FAIL outcomes remain retained. Missing preexisting anchors block only their dependent predicates; they never become invented success.",
    "No-spend claims are provisional until the explicit parent verifier joins the complete verified shutdown ledger, including rejected submissions and all reachable unmined ancestors.",
    "The extension is not automatically admitted by4.2 or any existing profile; no existing99/426 gate, policy or schema is changed."
  ],
  "evidenceRules": [
    "Exactly61 predicate IDs and exactly the declared ordered public requests; every complete argument object is independently bound.",
    "Every cryptographic ordinary control is independently authenticated using external peer/verifier fixture keys.",
    "Every recoverable returned transaction, including failed negative calls, is exposed for parent identity/storage/mined-root binding; no failed predicate excuses provenance.",
    "Basket mutations use isolated native source indices and a controlled external transaction; all transaction bytes, output indices and metadata are checked.",
    "Parent must compare embedded boundary/clauses/trust anchors and storage/submission snapshots to authoritative original evidence.",
    "Unknown native costs remain unknown; reference self-tests never qualify native behavior."
  ],
  "prospectiveCorrections": {
    "uppercaseIdentifiers": "BRC100 line307 explicitly says interoperability SDK identifier handling trims and lowercases. Preserve uppercase caller inputs; require exact normalized-basket state across create/internalize/list/relinquish. This changes only the four uppercase predicates prospectively.",
    "rejectedInternalizationPersistence": "For each malformed insertion, capture every independently owned Go provider before and after the exact public call. A complete unchanged identity/provider-scoped output snapshot is required for PASS. Missing observations are BLOCKED; any output state change despite a rejection is FAIL. Final parent joins the separate append-only observation ledger and complete owned provider registry.",
    "priorEvidence": "Oracle1 report, source and policy remain immutable; oracle2 observations are separate."
  },
